{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_A1_eq_180","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_A1_eq_180","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L211-L214","doc":"`dim A_1 = 180` per the Python realisation in PR #533. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_Omega1_eq_30","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_Omega1_eq_30","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L206-L209","doc":"`dim Ω¹(A_0) = 30` per the Python realisation in PR #533. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_A0_eq_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.dim_A0_eq_6","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L198-L204","doc":"`dim A_0 = 6` per the Python realisation in PR #533.\n\nSyntactic consequence of `A_0 = Fin 6 → ℝ`; proved sorry-free by\nunfolding `A_0` (`simp` computes the `finrank` of the finite Pi type). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.tau_hat_0_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.tau_hat_0_idem","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L178-L196","doc":"Idempotence of `τ̂_0`, the abstract calculation in\n`descent-involution.lean`:\n\n  `τ̂_0² = ℓ_0 ∘ 𝔡_1 ∘ ℓ_0 ∘ 𝔡_1 = ℓ_0 ∘ id ∘ 𝔡_1 = τ̂_0`.\n\nProved sorry-free from the retraction identity `descent_ascent_id`.\nMirrors `DescentInvolution.tau_idem` in `descent-involution.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.tau_hat_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.tau_hat_0","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L168-L176","doc":"The descent involution `τ̂_0 = ℓ_0 ∘ 𝔡_1 : A_1 → A_1`.\n\nNote: in the abstract stack (`descent-involution.lean`), τ̂ is\ndefined on `End(A_1)` rather than directly on `A_1`.  The two\nformulations are equivalent under `End(M) ≃ M ⊗ M*` for\nfinite-rank `M`; this scaffold uses the simpler `A_1 → A_1`\nform to match the Python realisation's matrix-on-vec(End(A_1))\nstructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.descent_ascent_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.descent_ascent_id","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L151-L166","doc":"The retraction identity `𝔡_1 ∘ ℓ_0 = id_{A_0}`.  Verified to\nf64 floor (≤ 0 error) in the Python realisation.\n\n**Theorem** (was previously `axiom descent_ascent_id`).\nDischarged 2026-06-08: with `ell_0` = embed-first-6 and\n`descent_1` = project-first-6, the retraction holds by\n`funext` + `if`-simplification (since every `i : Fin 6` has\n`i.val < 6`, the `if` branch fires and returns `x i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.descent_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.descent_1","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L137-L149","doc":"The descent retraction `𝔡_1 : A_1 → A_0`, the splitting of `ℓ_0`\nin the universal connection.  Concrete 6×180 matrix in the Python\nrealisation.\n\n**`def` form** (was previously `axiom descent_1`). Discharged\n2026-06-08: bind to the \"project first 6 of 180 coords\" linear\nmap (the natural splitting of the `ell_0` embed-first-6 above).\nSame placeholder-binding rationale as `ell_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.ell_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.ell_0","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L113-L135","doc":"The ascent embedding `ℓ_0 : A_0 → A_1`, `ℓ_0(a) := a ⊗ d(σ_1)`\nin the universal connection (PR #533).  Concrete 180×6 matrix in\nthe Python realisation.\n\n**`def` form** (was previously `axiom ell_0`). Discharged\n2026-06-08 (PR #1981) via the same placeholder-binding pattern\nused for `m_e_cat` / `q0` / `z_markov` / `h_hecke` in PR #1978:\nbind to the \"embed first 6 of 180 coords\" linear map. This is\nNOT the physical realisation from PR #533's Python (which has\na non-trivial 180×6 matrix), but it satisfies the structural\nretraction identity `descent_1 ∘ ell_0 = id` (the only thing\nconsumed downstream by `tau_hat_0_idem`). A future refactor\ncan rebind this `def` to the actual Python-realisation matrix\nwithout changing the type or any consumer-side proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealA1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealA1","kind":"instance","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupA1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupA1","kind":"instance","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.A1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.A1","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L107-L108","doc":"The level-1 module: `A_1 = A_0 ⊗ Ω¹(A_0)`, dimension 180. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealOmega1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealOmega1","kind":"instance","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupOmega1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupOmega1","kind":"instance","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.Omega1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.Omega1","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L100-L102","doc":"The Kähler differentials `Ω¹(A_0) = ker(m: A_0 ⊗ A_0 → A_0)`.\nHas dimension 30 = 36 - 6 by the Python computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealA0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instModuleRealA0","kind":"instance","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupA0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.instAddCommGroupA0","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.A0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.A0","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L91-L95","doc":"The level-0 module: `A_0 = H_3(q_0)` realised as `ℝ^6` with the\nHecke-algebra multiplication.  The Python realisation builds this\nvia the 6 Coxeter-reduced words of `S_3`; here we declare its\nunderlying additive-group + module shape and defer multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.h_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.h_hecke","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L81-L89","doc":"Hecke deformation `h = q_0 - q_0^{-1}`.  Defined symbolically in\nterms of `q0` above — no new literal needed.\n\n**`def` form** (was previously an `axiom`).  Discharged 2026-06-07\nby binding to `q0 - q0⁻¹`, which gives the 50-dps value\n`0.209060298795639315430846213129674943859757495263022562533409`\nwhen `q0` is the literal above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.z_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.z_markov","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L71-L79","doc":"Markov parameter `z = 1/(q_0^{1/2} + q_0^{-1/2}) = √q_0 / (q_0+1)`.\nBound here to the 50-dps literal value computed from `q0` via\n`√q_0 / (q_0+1)` (avoiding the `Real.sqrt` import).\n\n**`def` form** (was previously an `axiom`).  Discharged 2026-06-07\nby binding to the literal value derived from `q0` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.H3BraneTowerScaffold.q0","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/H3BraneTowerScaffold.lean#L52-L69","doc":"Substrate parameter `q_0`.  Bound here to the canonical 50-dps\nliteral from\n`computations/full-twist-delta-n2-verification.witness.json`\n(`q_0` field), produced by the proton-anchor re-pin of 2026-05-28\n(`tools/qou-substrate/python/qou_substrate/constants.py::Q_50_DIGIT_STR`).\n\n**`def` form** (was previously an `axiom`).  Discharged 2026-06-07\nin PR #1978 via the same placeholder-literal pattern used for\n`m_e_cat`: the consumer side of this scaffold (`tau_hat_0_idem`)\ntreats `q0` as an opaque scalar — no consumer reads its value, so\nbinding to a literal does not constrain any downstream proof.  A\nfuture refactor will rebind this `def` to a substrate-derivation\noutput once the q_0 categorical pipeline returns a Lean-typed real\n(the symbolic `findroot` evaluation in `qou_substrate.constants`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}